# The overlay ships to a game server that is almost always Linux, and the NPC
# script is mounted or copied straight into rAthena's npc/custom/ directory.
# core.autocrlf=true on a Windows clone would rewrite these to CRLF on
# checkout, putting a stray \r after `FAKE_NPC,{` and after every label.
# Pin them to LF so the artifact an operator receives is the artifact that was
# tested, whatever platform they cloned on.
#
# The globs below use `**/` and not a bare `/`: a fnmatch `*` does not cross
# a directory separator, so `overlay/*.txt` covered the Tier 1 overlay and
# silently missed overlay/tier2/ro_admin_tier2.txt -- the artifact most
# likely of all of them to be copied onto a Linux server. `a/**/b` matches
# zero or more intervening directories, so these still cover overlay/ itself.
overlay/**/*.txt text eol=lf
overlay/**/*.sql text eol=lf

# Same reason for the Tier 2 hook: these two files are pasted into rAthena's
# src/custom/ on the build host. g++ tolerates CRLF, but the artifact an
# operator receives should be byte-for-byte the one that was compile-checked.
overlay/**/*.inc text eol=lf
